Technical
### Changed

- Update Anthropic to 12.53.0, coverlet.collector to 10.1.0 and Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI to 10.10.1. ([#328](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/328))

### Added

- **Breaking:** Remove `description` from `changelog.json`, now schema version 2, and keep the complete facts, descriptions included, in a new `facts` array in the run record. ([#294](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/294))
- **Breaking:** Make `preview` free of model calls: show the facts, the dropped changes with their reasons, and what `generate` would send, without needing a key. ([#292](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/292))
- Open each run's summary on how the run went, add a `chartula · <command>` header, and group the help text. ([#342](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/342))
- Group the `doctor` checks into Repository, Model and GitHub, mark each status with a symbol and word, and make the verdict say what warnings mean for a run. ([#341](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/341))
- Show run progress with the Quiet Pulse spinner on a live terminal and add the `--plain` option to every command. ([#340](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/340))
- Quote pull request titles and descriptions between `<title>` and `<description>` tags in prompts, and cut descriptions longer than 8,000 characters. ([#338](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/338))
- Stop `generate` before the first model call when the release is already published, unless `--replace-published` is passed. ([#335](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/335))
- Name this version's config template in the `doctor` output when no `chartula.yaml` is found. ([#329](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/329))
- Show each step of a run on stderr while it works, rewriting the line in place on a terminal and printing one plain line per step otherwise. ([#297](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/297))
- Add the `chartula doctor` command, which checks the setup a run needs, one line per check, and exits 1 when a check fails. ([#295](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/295))
- Take closed issue numbers from the text the model reads at every `factBase.depth`, and read the old value `title-description-and-issues` as `title-and-description`. ([#293](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/293))
- Render a commit without a pull request as its own change next to the pull requests, and skip merge commits that have none. ([#291](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/291))
- Add `chartula --version`, which prints the installed informational version and exits 0 without needing a checkout, configuration, key or token. ([#286](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/286))
- Render a first tag from the first commit without `--whole-history`, and confirm a first tag or a range above `range.confirmAboveCommits` before anything is read. ([#282](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/282))

### Fixed

- Fix the help text so that each option is listed once under its group, with `--replace-published` under "What a run writes". ([#344](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/344))
- Fix the rule-based faithfulness check to compare names with whitespace folded and code fences removed, so wrapped names and fenced blocks are no longer wrongly flagged. ([#336](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/336))
- Write a fixed sentence into `CHANGELOG.md` and the release notes when a release has nothing for the technical reader, instead of an empty heading. ([#333](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/333))
- Escape only what JSON requires when writing `changelog.json` and the run record, so backticks and non-ASCII characters stay readable. ([#332](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/332))
- Set the review flags apart from the last entry of a rendering with a blank line and a `Flagged for review:` heading. ([#331](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/331))
- Say `unauthenticated, <VARIABLE> is not set` in the run header when a credential variable is unset or blank. ([#330](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/330))
- Refuse unknown or misused options before a run starts, and honour `--help` after a command. ([#301](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/301))
- Append the trailing slash to a GitHub API base URL written without one. ([#290](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/290))
- Read an empty `filter.excludeCategories` list as dropping no category instead of keeping the default. ([#289](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/289))
- Report a model answer the SDK cannot read as unreadable instead of as unreachable. ([#288](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/288))
- Refuse a directory that holds both `chartula.yaml` and `chartula.yml`, naming both paths. ([#287](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/287))
- Check that the token may publish before the first model call of `generate`, using `POST releases/generate-notes`. ([#285](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/285))
- Correct the `--no-publish` help text to say that every file is written and only the GitHub release notes are not published. ([#284](https://github.com/goldbarth/chartula/pull/284))

